<title>CANADA: Imperial Oil lowers posted oil prices.</title>
<headline>Imperial Oil lowers posted oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Oil Ltd said it lowered the price it would pay for some grades of crude oil by C$5.00/cubic metre or C$0.79/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Edmonton light sweet C$202.00/cubic metre, or C$32.12/barrel</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$196.00/cubic metre, or C$31.16/barrel</p>
<p>Bow River at Hardisty C$169.00/cubic metre, or C$26.87/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$178.00/cubic metre, or C$28.30/barrel</p>
<p>-- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
</text>
